compatibility.md has no row for it. Row :18 covers Claude Desktop only through the plugin or a skill upload. Row :28 points MCP clients to mcp/README.md, which gives no status for Claude Desktop.

The only Claude Desktop check is manual-checks.md:74-83, and none of its boxes is ticked. plan.md:186 lists it as an owner task after the build, and no file records a result.

What has been checked: the packed server starts and lists its tools under Node, in pack-mcpb.mjs:72-80 and in the reviewer's runs.

What hasn't been checked:
- Claude Desktop's install dialog;
- running the bundle on its built-in Node;
- whether forms appear.

The owner's rule is to label unverified surfaces, and this one has no label. D25 makes the Claude Code smoke test required before the PR, but doesn't mention this check. So the first release can ship the bundle without anyone opening it in Claude Desktop.

D26 and plan.md:135 set the floor at Node 22.19. Finding 45's recorded fix changes only CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/publishing.md. Five more places state the floor:
- manifest.json:61: ">=20.0.0";
- manifests.test.ts:101, which pins that value, so it keeps passing when package.json changes;
- bundle.mjs:22: target 'node20';
- mcp/README.md:48: 'needs Node.js 20 or later';
- mcp/README.md:177: 'the server itself runs on Node.js 20+'.

Suppose only package.json's engines, manifests.test.ts:36 and the CI matrix change. Then the npm package says >=22.19, while the MCPB and the README promise Node 20, which no CI job runs any more.

Today the Node 20 claim holds for the bundle: the packed server ran on Node 20.0.0, in both protocol eras, on both the form path and the text path.

Not checked: which Node Claude Desktop bundles, so whether a higher floor in the manifest could block installs.

